.TH "GLESHA-RESTORE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-restore \- restore a snapshot into a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha restore\fR SET \-\-into DIR [options]
.br
\fBglesha restore\fR SET \-\-cancel [\-\-into DIR] [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Restore a snapshot of SET, by default the latest, into DIR. DIR may exist; existing files are never replaced. An incremental snapshot is restored together with the snapshots it depends on.
.PP
Archives are read from local copies when possible, otherwise from the remotes in \-\-from order. Objects in cold storage must be retrieved first, which may be charged; this is confirmed interactively or with \-\-request\-retrieval.
.PP
With \-\-cancel, unfinished restore tasks of SET are dropped, optionally only those for DIR. Restored files and downloaded data are kept, and retrievals already requested continue.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-into DIR
Restore into DIR; with \-\-cancel, limit to DIR.
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot ID
Snapshot ID, or 'latest' (default: latest).
.TP
.B \-\-cancel
Cancel unfinished restore tasks.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Read from REMOTE, in order (default: set's remotes).
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the archive passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). A trailing newline is ignored. Without this option, the passphrase is read from a hidden prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-archive\-passphrase\-file ID=FILE
Read the passphrase of snapshot ID from FILE. Use it when the snapshots of an incremental chain have different passphrases. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.SS Retrieval options
.TP
.B \-\-request\-retrieval
Allow charged cold retrieval without asking.
.TP
.B \-\-retrieval TIER
Tier: bulk, standard, or expedited (default: bulk). The default comes from the [cold] tier setting.
.TP
.B \-\-days N
Keep retrieved copies for N days (default: 3). The default comes from the [cold] days setting. A pending request keeps its original duration.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory, or 128MiB). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. On Linux, the default is half of the available memory. On other systems, or if the available memory cannot be read, the default is 128MiB.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Run up to N transfers at once (default: 4). The memory limit may lower the effective number.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Hash up to N files at once (default: 4).
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha restore docs \-\-into ~/recovered
glesha restore docs \-\-snapshot ID \-\-into .
glesha restore docs \-\-cancel
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-browse (1),
.BR glesha\-history (1)
